  "discussion": "A north-northwest swell will continue a slow decline through Saturday, and surf along exposed north and west facing shores should drop below High Surf Advisory thresholds this afternoon or evening. A reinforcing medium period energy out of the north-northwest (330 to 340 degree) should arrive late Saturday into Sunday. Surf could approach advisory thresholds during its peak early Sunday morning. Another large northwest to north-northwest swell is Wednesday or Thursday of next week. A small south-southwest swell should produce south shore surf slightly above seasonal average through Saturday. A tiny pulse from the south-southeast may maintain surf near seasonal average Sunday and Monday, followed by background level surf through the remainder of the week. Surf along east-facing shores will stay elevated and choppy through much of the week due to the strong trades. Select northeast exposures should see long-period energy from the large north-northwest swell into tonight.",
